Subject: [PATCH] Micro-optimizations: position hashing, light BFS allocation,
 farmland water scan

Three low-risk wins ported from Beast (HomoMC) 1.12.2:

- BaseBlockPosition#hashCode is cached (NONE sentinel so a legitimate hash of
  0 still works); MutableBlockPosition overrides it to always recompute
  since its coordinates change. BlockPosition is a HashMap key in hot paths
  such as Chunk.tileEntities lookups on every block update.

- The two light BFS loops in World#updateBrightness now reuse one
  MutableBlockPosition instead of allocating a BlockPosition per visited
  node. World#m(IWorldAccess dispatch) hands listeners an immutable copy so
  the reuse can never leak into external code.

- BlockSoil's nearby-water scan replaces the mutable-position iterator and
  per-position World#getType with plain loops, one chunk lookup per column
  and a direct Chunk#getBlockData (which bounds-checks y and returns AIR).
  The 9x9x2 search volume is unchanged; based on Tuinity's version.

Verified: 200k random coordinate triples produce identical hashes for both
immutable and mutable positions (including the all-zero case).

